### What the page covers

Replaced the bootstrap stub with a full handbook page aligned to `det-motion-prefers-reduced.check.js` and sibling page `det-motion-no-auto-play-flash.md`:

| Section | Content |
|---------|---------|
| **Purpose** | PDCA framing; Playwright emulates `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`; four violation kinds; essential-motion exceptions (`spinner`, `loading`, `skeleton`, `progress`, `aria-busy`, `role="status"`/`progressbar`) |
| **Passing signals** | Theme `@media` blocks in `forge-theme.css`, `forge-ambient.css`, `ks-living-background.css`, `script-assembly.css`; static pulses/breathe/tilt; no autoplay video/SMIL |
| **Failing signals** | Active `.pulse-amber`, `.breathe-*` transitions, `.forge-card` transitions, autoplay video, SMIL, missing media queries |
| **Before example** | Failing: `.pulse-amber`, `.breathe-link`, `.breathe-static`, custom `ks-float` animation, `<video autoplay>` — no reduced-motion override |
| **After example** | Passing: `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` disables decorative motion; static `.glass` / `.forge-card`; essential `.spinner-border` with `aria-busy="true"`; static poster `<img>` |
| **Evidence and remediation** | `motionPrefersReducedReport` fields; violation kind table; six-step remediation; harness commands |
| **Related rules** | `DET.MOTION.NO_AUTO_PLAY_FLASH`, `AI.MOTION.INTENTIONALITY`, `AI.AMBIENT.READABILITY_CONFLICT` |

